From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 02:37:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/haswell: Boot options for the payload

The ouroBIOS EDK2 payload reads two boot switches of the setup for
both boards, as UINT32 variables of the coreboot options GUID, and a
missing variable counts as on: today the W541 always gets the default.
They go into General > Boot with iPXE and CSMWrap, as on the M920x.

- usb_boot, "Boot from USB drives", default on: off, the boot manager
  no longer lists the USB drives of the laptop and the dock. The help
  says how they can still boot (entries made by an OS, the UEFI Shell
  and its startup.nsh, CSMWrap, Boot From File, and PlatformRecovery
  with \EFI\BOOT\BOOTX64.EFI), that a capsule on a USB drive still
  installs, and that it is not a security setting.
- boot_menu_prompt, "Boot menu prompt", default on: off, no "Press
  ESC" line on the logo, and Esc still opens the boot menu, from the
  internal keyboard too.

The help names the equivalents as in the ThinkPad setup (USB UEFI BIOS
Support, Option Key Display): the names come from the T540p/W540 user
guide, not from a W541 one. The Boot form, hidden in builds without
iPXE and CSMWrap, now always shows on the W541.

The option ROM setting of the M920x is not added: EDK2_LOAD_OPTION_ROMS
stays off on the W541, so the payload has no PciPlatformDxe to read it.
The VBIOS of the NVIDIA GPU in CBFS is a legacy image only, for the
ACPI _ROM, and the only other card that could bring a ROM is an
ExpressCard, whose unsigned code would then run in the firmware with
Secure Boot off by default.

The T440p shares the menu and keeps it as it is: both options are
suppressed there, and the form keeps its condition.

TEST=Host syntax check of cfr.c with the W541 mrc config and a T440p
one; tools/cfr-dump.sh for mrc and nri: the menu is valid, with both
options in Boot, and every help line under 60 columns; the CFR record
is 23568 bytes, against a coreboot table of 32 KiB. The payload code
(edk2/0037) has not run on a W541 yet. For the W541 hardware test: the
first boot with no variable lists USB drives and shows the prompt;
off, a USB stick in a laptop and in a dock port leaves the boot order
and the boot menu while the internal drives, the Shell, iPXE and
CSMWrap stay, and Esc on the internal keyboard still opens the boot
menu without the prompt.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c | 43 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 40 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
index 4395304b8a..c48f540a87 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
@@ -226,7 +226,8 @@ static const struct sm_object general_about = SM_DECLARE_FORM({
 
 /*
  * The boot options of the payload: its boot manager reads them (EDK2,
- * PlatformBootManagerLib), coreboot does not.
+ * PlatformBootManagerLib), coreboot does not. A missing variable counts as
+ * on there.
  */
 static const struct sm_object ipxe_boot = SM_DECLARE_BOOL({
 	.flags		= CONFIG(EDK2_ENABLE_IPXE) ? 0 : CFR_OPTFLAG_SUPPRESS,
@@ -250,13 +251,49 @@ static const struct sm_object csmwrap_boot = SM_DECLARE_BOOL({
 	.default_value	= true,
 });
 
+/* W541: the T440p keeps its menu */
+static const struct sm_object usb_boot = SM_DECLARE_BOOL({
+	.flags		= CONFIG(BOARD_LENOVO_THINKPAD_W541) ? 0 : CFR_OPTFLAG_SUPPRESS,
+	.opt_name	= "usb_boot",
+	.ui_name	= "Boot from USB drives",
+	.ui_helptext	= "The USB drives (laptop and dock ports) in the boot order\n"
+			  "and the boot menu.\n"
+			  "Off: the firmware does not list them, but they can still\n"
+			  "boot: from the entries that an OS made, from the UEFI\n"
+			  "Shell and its startup.nsh, from CSMWrap, from Boot From\n"
+			  "File in the setup's Boot Maintenance Manager, and through\n"
+			  "\\EFI\\BOOT\\BOOTX64.EFI, which the firmware tries on every\n"
+			  "drive once no boot entry works (PlatformRecovery). An\n"
+			  "update capsule on a USB drive still installs.\n"
+			  "Not a security setting: with Secure Boot on, these paths\n"
+			  "start only signed programs, and the default keys accept\n"
+			  "those signed by Microsoft (Windows, shim).\n"
+			  "Default: on, as USB UEFI BIOS Support in the ThinkPad\n"
+			  "setup.",
+	.default_value	= true,
+});
+
+static const struct sm_object boot_menu_prompt = SM_DECLARE_BOOL({
+	.flags		= CONFIG(BOARD_LENOVO_THINKPAD_W541) ? 0 : CFR_OPTFLAG_SUPPRESS,
+	.opt_name	= "boot_menu_prompt",
+	.ui_name	= "Boot menu prompt",
+	.ui_helptext	= "\"Press ESC for Boot Options/Settings\" on the logo at\n"
+			  "startup. Off: the line is not shown, and Esc still opens\n"
+			  "the boot menu, from the keyboard of the laptop too.\n"
+			  "Default: on, as Option Key Display in the ThinkPad setup.",
+	.default_value	= true,
+});
+
+/* Always shown on the W541: usb_boot and boot_menu_prompt are in every EDK2 build */
 static const struct sm_object general_boot = SM_DECLARE_FORM({
-	.flags		= (CONFIG(EDK2_ENABLE_IPXE) || CONFIG(EDK2_ENABLE_CSMWRAP))
-			  ? 0 : CFR_OPTFLAG_SUPPRESS,
+	.flags		= (CONFIG(BOARD_LENOVO_THINKPAD_W541) || CONFIG(EDK2_ENABLE_IPXE) ||
+			   CONFIG(EDK2_ENABLE_CSMWRAP)) ? 0 : CFR_OPTFLAG_SUPPRESS,
 	.ui_name	= "Boot",
 	.obj_list	= (const struct sm_object *[]) {
 		&ipxe_boot,
 		&csmwrap_boot,
+		&usb_boot,
+		&boot_menu_prompt,
 		NULL
 	},
 });
-- 
2.47.3

